# Code quality

## Layering (SOLID)

- **S:** Components render · use-cases orchestrate · `<module>-adapter.ts` transports · `<module>-errors|labels.ts` map DTO → UI · client UI stores (Zustand) hold chrome only.
- **O:** Extend via new mappers/modules — don’t edit the HTTP client for every screen.
- **L:** Real + fake port impls honor the same types.
- **I:** Small ports (`RenewalsReader`, auth, gym-orgs) — not one god `Api`.
- **D:** UI/use-cases depend on ports; wire at `<module>-services.ts`, spread by `lib/api/composition.ts`.

## Habits

- Factory-inject deps; no hidden fetch globals in features.
- Validate at adapter boundary (Zod); no cast-and-pray.
- Endpoint paths in `modules/<module>/<module>-endpoints.ts` — no scattered magic strings.
- Strict TypeScript; no `any` (use `unknown` + a type guard, or a generic); glossary names from `docs/CONTEXT.md`.
- Calm errors in UI — never stack traces.
- Choose **state tier** before coding (`state-management.mdc`) — do not default to a global client store.

## Style

- Early returns; avoid nesting beyond 2 levels.
- Extract functions longer than ~30 lines into named helpers.
- Booleans prefixed `is` / `has` / `should` (`isInvited`, `hasActiveGrant`).
- **Named exports only** — no default exports for components, hooks, or utilities.
- Every exported function has an explicit return type — don’t rely on inference for public surfaces.
- Comment **why**, never what. (“snapshot price to avoid retroactive billing changes”.)
- Composition over inheritance; no class hierarchies.
- Do not add a dependency or a new pattern (state manager, form lib, data-fetching lib) that isn’t already in `package.json` without asking first — see `001-tech-stack.mdc`.
